Done. `pipeline_refactored.py` is the new file. Here's what changed:

### What changed, and why

| Problem in original | Fix |
|---|---|
| `DB_PATH = "metrics.db"`, `DB_PASS = "password123"` hardcoded as module constants | All config sourced from `os.environ` — `DB_USER` / `DB_PASS` have no default (fail-fast if unset) |
| `"INSERT INTO errors VALUES ('%s', '%s', %d)" % (...)` — string interpolation of user data | Parameterised queries with `?` placeholders via `executemany` |
| All logic in one 110-line `proc_data()` function | Split into **Extract**: `parse_log_line` / `extract_logs` → **Transform**: `summarize_errors` / `compute_api_averages` / `track_active_sessions` → **Load**: `init_db` / `persist_*` / `generate_html_report` / `write_report` |
| `line.split(" ")`, manual index arithmetic, concatenation loops for message reconstruction | Two compiled regexes (`_LOG_HEADER_RE`, `_USER_RE`, `_API_RE`) with named groups |
| No type hints, no docstrings | Full type annotations (Python 3.14 syntax: `str \| None`, `list[LogRecord]`) and docstrings on every function + dataclass |

### Output verification

The HTML report is byte-identical in content to the original (same sections, same `<li>` / `<tr>` data, same rounding). The only addition is `<!DOCTYPE html>` for valid HTML5 — the original produced a non-standard document.
